   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# regions from masks: patch existing regions\n\n1. The **sample facade** node gives the picture and the mask folder the base regions are read from.\n2. The new shape here is a rectangle made with core mask nodes. Your own: paint the shapes into one PNG (white on black, or alpha), put it in ComfyUI/input and use Load Image (as Mask) instead.\n3. From Masks, `split_masks = balcony`: every separate shape becomes `balcony_01`, `balcony_02` ... in group `balcony`.\n   `on_top` cuts them out of the regions below; `underneath` would only fill pixels no region has.\n4. New regions are tagged with the region they were cut from (and its tags), so `[tag:W_F1_*]` reaches a shape painted into a floor 1 window.\n5. Plug the plan into a region sampler (see facade_regions_diffusion).\n\nSeveral separate masks instead (SAM, Illustrator layers): batch them (Batch Masks) and write one name per line, `name = group` sets the group.\n"
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  },
